    "file": "world/sources/catalogue/places-imperial-fringe.json",
    "path": "places[place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station].why.founding"
   },
   "text": "Claywater Station is a mixed village where the road crosses the Claywater ford. An Imperial well and station house stand on one bank of the ford. An Argonian landing stands on the other bank. The landing is older than the station. Argonian polers worked the ford before the Imperials dug the well. A poler's canoe lies pulled up on the bank.",
   "confirmed": {
    "sha": "4cab7b8862dc",
    "note": "Station house and stone well on one bank, the mud huts and the landing stage on the other, one canoe beached by the polers' hut.",
    "ids": [
     "place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station.parcel.claywater-station.polers-hut.assembly.canoe"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "promise.claywater-station.prose-why-occupantsmotive",
   "kind": "prose",
   "source": {
    "file": "world/sources/catalogue/places-imperial-fringe.json",
    "path": "places[place.imperial-fringe.claywater-station].why.occupantsMotive"
   },
   "text": "Two communities share the village because neither can hold the other's half.",
   "confirmed": {
    "sha": "2e3c59874c48",
    "note": "Two halves built as two groups of buildings across the ford."
   }
  },
  {
